1028 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1027 0 R
  /Alt (This image displays three comparative maps and a common legend, illustrating different stages of Protected Area (PA) land cover classification for the year 2021, alongside Very High Resolution (VHR) false-colour imagery. The geographic area shown is centered around Lat: 47.812789, Lon: 16.653742 (near Parndorf, Austria). All maps share a scale bar showing 0, 0.5, and 1 km, with a ratio of 1:10.000, and include a north arrow. The three map panels are: 1. **PA2021 L1-L4 TIF**: This map shows a detailed land cover classification in a TIFF format, labeled as Protected Areas (PA) for 2021, representing classification levels 1 through 4. It features numerous small, intricate polygons. 2. **PA2021 L4 GPKG**: This map displays a more generalized land cover classification for Protected Areas (PA) in 2021, specifically level 4, stored in a GeoPackage (GPKG) format. Compared to the L1-L4 TIF map, polygons are larger and appear geometrically simplified, with fewer small linear features. 3. **VHR False Colour 2021**: This panel presents Very High Resolution satellite imagery from 2021 in false colour, showing the actual ground truth with visible agricultural fields, forest patches, and other land features, serving as a reference for the land cover classifications. The 'PA2021 Legend' below the maps lists 48 different numerical land cover class codes (e.g., 1110, 1120, 1210, 2110, 2120, 3110, 4110, 5100, 6100, 7110, 8110, 8310), each associated with a distinct colour. The specific land cover type descriptions corresponding to these numerical codes are not provided within the image. The comparison highlights how different classification levels and processing methods (e.g., aggregation for GPKG format) can impact the geometric representation of land cover, particularly in relation to the level of detail captured (like Minimum Mapping Unit coherence) when delineating Protected Areas and other land use/land cover features.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [3]
  /Pg 1732 0 R
>>
endobj

